; The bidder's plan after the first lead. Winning 42 p. 9 (S-0022-a: plan for
; the setters holding the missing trumps), pp. 23-29 (S-0038-b,
; S-0039-b, S-0039-c: the six-trey off goes early, before a void setter can
; add count to it, S-0041-b: the top trump so the partner knows the trick is
; safe, S-0041-d, S-0041-f, S-0042-b, S-0042-c: Hand 12 played out, S-0043-c,
; S-0043-e, S-0044-b, S-0047-c, S-0047-d), pp. 11, 18-19 and 24 (S-0024-a,
; S-0033-b, S-0034-b, S-0040-b, S-0040-d: pull in count before the offs when
; the partner has one trump or none, or a double stands ahead of an off),
; p. 31 (S-0052-a), pp. 60-63 (S-0085-a, S-0086-a, S-0087-a),
; pp. 75-81 (S-0104-a, S-0105-c, S-0105-d, S-0107-b, S-0107-c, S-0109-b,
; S-0110-c), pp. 91-95 (S-0121-d, S-0122-b, S-0122-c, S-0122-e, S-0126-d),
; and the worked deals, Hands 12, 14, 15, 16, 23 to 26 and 28 to 35
; (S-0046-b, S-0046-c, S-0048-a, S-0051-c, S-0052-b, S-0107-d, S-0130-a,
; S-0130-d, S-0131-c, S-0134-c, S-0136-c, S-0137-a, S-0142-h, S-0142-k,
; S-0144-g, S-0144-k, S-0145-a, S-0146-e, S-0148-b, S-0148-i). The bidder's
; four steps (p. 26), in our words: trumps in; then, if it helps,
; one trump more for the partner's count, or the off's double first for its
; count; then the offs; then back in to take the rest.
; Rule, in our words, the bidder on lead after trick one, not in a crisis
; (crisis.silas):
; - while a setter may hold a trump, lead the highest trump still out;
; - once no trump is out, lead the highest trump once more if count is still
;   out and the partner has not yet had a trump trick to give it on; but keep
;   a trump until after the offs, unless all you hold besides it is winners
;   and one off, which can go last (Hand 33 trick 5);
; - holding a trump to win the lead back (and a bid of points): lead at once
;   the off whose own suit's double you lack, the one that risks least count,
;   its own and what it calls for (Hand 28 trick 3: the 3-1, which risks a
;   five, not the 5-3's ten; Hand 24 trick 3, S-0107-d: the 5-1, not the
;   6-4, a ten itself, which the 5-1 makes safe by drawing the 6-5),
;   or a double of another suit that may pull its count (a permission: Hands
;   8, 9 and 14 propose it, Hand 32 trick 3 leads the off); once every off has
;   its double, the double first (Hand 30 trick 5, the last trump the
;   partner's);
; - with no trump to win the lead back, in a bid of marks, or at no trump: the
;   off goes last. Take your other winners first (a double that may draw an
;   off's count from another suit among them), then the double of the off's
;   own suit next-to-last (Hands 16, 17, 18, 19, 25, 26, 28, 34, 35).
; Replaces gates/c01a-top-trump-for-the-donation.silas and
; gates/c11-double-ahead-of-the-off.silas. How it differs: C1a reads the
; bidder's knowledge (partner shown void, a trump out); the book leads the top
; trump for the partner whenever the partner cannot know the trick is safe
; any other way: with the partner not shown void (Hands 12, 15, 23, 26, 28,
; 30) and with no trump out (Hands 15, 23, 33). C11 takes only the double of
; the off's own suit and fires the moment trumps are drawn; the book also
; leads another suit's double for the off's count (Hands 8, 9, 14, 18, 23),
; strips first and saves the off's double for next-to-last when it cannot win
; the lead back (Hands 16, 17, 18, 19, 25, 26), dumps a bare off before the
; double ahead of another (Hand 28 trick 3, where C11 leads the 6-6), and
; leads the double with the last trump in the partner's hand (Hand 30).
; GAP knowledge: the donation lead's condition is what the partner can know
; (S-0041-b and S-0047-d state it: the partner gives count only when he knows
; the bidder wins, and he knows only on the highest trump still out); this
; file reads it as the partner not yet having discarded on one of the
; bidder's trump leads, and no trump out at all (a trump out with the
; partner, as in Hand 30, means he must follow). S-0040-d's first case, "the
; partner has one trump or none", is the same reading from the bidder's
; side: a partner with one trump is a donor after one trump lead.
; The book contradicts itself on keeping the last trump. Hand 13 (S-0044-b,
; p. 27) keeps it rather than fish for the partner's count, stating as a rule
; that a trump stays until the offs are gone; Hand 33 (S-0144-k, p. 111) leads
; it for the donation while holding the 2-1 off. This file encodes Hand 33 (a
; full deal; Hand 13's first two tricks are not given): the last trump may go
; when the rest of the hand is winners and one off.

(include book)

(policy bidders-plan
  (rule draw-the-trumps (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (on-lead b)
    (not (trick-number 1))
    (not (crisis))
    (not (no-setter-trump))
    (own-legal lead)
    (boss-trump lead))
  (rule the-donation-lead (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (on-lead b)
    (not (trick-number 1))
    (bidders-partner p)
    (not (trump-out))
    (own-legal lead)
    (boss-trump lead)
    (some (roles out) (live out) (not (mine out)) (count-tile out))
    (none (roles l his) (led b l) (trump-tile l) (played-to l p his) (not (trump-tile his)))
    (or
      (some (roles other) (mine other) (trump-tile other) (not (tile other lead)))
      (none (roles o o2) (off o) (off o2))))
  (rule dump-a-bare-off-calling-no-count (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (on-lead b)
    (no-setter-trump)
    (not (every-trick))
    (some (roles kept) (mine kept) (trump-tile kept))
    (own-legal lead)
    (bare-off lead)
    (count lead 0)
    (not (calls-for-count lead)))
  (rule dump-a-bare-off-calling-a-five (play lead)
    (pattern
      (viewer b)
      (bidder b)
      (on-lead b)
      (no-setter-trump)
      (not (every-trick))
      (some (roles kept) (mine kept) (trump-tile kept))
      (own-legal lead)
      (bare-off lead)
      (or
        (and (count lead 0) (not (calls-for lead 10)))
        (and (count lead 5) (not (calls-for-count lead)))))
    (pattern
      (viewer b)
      (bidder b)
      (on-lead b)
      (no-setter-trump)
      (not (every-trick))
      (some (roles kept) (mine kept) (trump-tile kept))
      (own-legal lead)
      (some (roles o) (bare-off o) (not (calls-for o 10)) (draws-the-count-for lead o))))
  (rule dump-a-bare-off (play lead)
    (pattern
      (viewer b)
      (bidder b)
      (on-lead b)
      (no-setter-trump)
      (not (every-trick))
      (some (roles kept) (mine kept) (trump-tile kept))
      (own-legal lead)
      (bare-off lead))
    (pattern
      (viewer b)
      (bidder b)
      (on-lead b)
      (no-setter-trump)
      (not (every-trick))
      (some (roles kept) (mine kept) (trump-tile kept))
      (own-legal lead)
      (some (roles o) (bare-off o) (draws-the-count-for lead o))))
  (rule the-double-ahead-of-the-off (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (on-lead b)
    (no-setter-trump)
    (not (every-trick))
    (some (roles kept) (mine kept) (trump-tile kept))
    (own-legal lead)
    (protects lead off))
  (rule cash-the-other-winners (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (on-lead b)
    (no-setter-trump)
    (or (none (roles t) (mine t) (trump-tile t)) (every-trick))
    (some (roles o) (off o))
    (own-legal lead)
    (not (can-lose lead))
    (none (roles o) (off o) (strips-the-suit-of lead o)))
  (rule the-double-of-the-offs-suit (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (on-lead b)
    (no-setter-trump)
    (or (none (roles t) (mine t) (trump-tile t)) (every-trick))
    (own-legal lead)
    (double lead)
    (off off)
    (strips-the-suit-of lead off))
  (rule take-the-rest (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (on-lead b)
    (no-setter-trump)
    (none (roles o) (off o))
    (own-legal lead)
    (not (can-lose lead))))
